content.text:
Part "Store shell" is clean: `./make.sh` reports 738 placed, with no REFUSED or OFF-PALETTE lines. I didn't change `parts/shell.mjs`.

The off-palette blocks come from the roof step. The roof tool lays them from `roof.json` (the `modern` preset) right after the shell, and `./make.sh` labels that line "fix roof.json". They are `smooth_stone_stairs` ×40, `andesite_slab` ×40 and `stone_slab` ×64. `roof.json` belongs to the roofs part, so I left it alone. The build still produced a whole `build.nbt`.

```json
{
  "summary": "Store shell part builds cleanly (738 blocks placed) with no refused writes or off-palette blocks. The off-palette stairs and slabs reported by make.sh come from the roof tool's modern preset in roof.json, not from shell.mjs. No change made.",
  "waste": [
    {
      "what": "Worked out that the off-palette report belonged to the roof step rather than the shell, by running make.sh and reading roof.json.",
      "cost": "1 build run plus 1 file read",
      "tool": "make.sh could attribute off-palette blocks to the module that wrote them (roof tool vs part) instead of printing them on the roof line. A `--palette` option for `mcd roof` or the modern preset would remove the off-palette blocks at the source."
    }
  ],
  "companions": [
    {
      "role": "roofer",
      "task": "Map the modern preset's smooth_stone_stairs, andesite_slab and stone_slab onto palette.json blocks (polished_andesite_stairs / polished_andesite_slab / smooth_stone_slab) in roof.json or the roof spec."
    }
  ],
  "finished": true,
  "left": [
    "roof.json (modern preset) still emits off-palette smooth_stone_stairs x40, andesite_slab x40, stone_slab x64; the roofs part must fix that"
  ]
}
```
